## Method

- **Workloads:** GET only, SET only, mixed (alternating SET and GET).
- **Keys:** {{ method.key_space }} keys (`k0` to `k{{ method.key_space - 1 }}`), all filled with a known value before every run, so GETs always find a value and the map does not grow during a run.
- **Values:** {{ method.value_description }}
- **Clients:** closed loop (each client waits for a reply before sending the next request). Client counts: {{ method.clients_list }}.
- **Timing:** each request is timed from just before it is written until its reply line is read. Requests per second is total requests divided by the wall-clock time from when all clients are connected until the last reply. Filling, command generation and connecting are outside the clock.
- **Repeats:** {{ method.warmup }} Then {{ method.sweeps }} sweeps of every run, {{ method.pause_secs }} s pause between runs. Each cell is the **median** of the {{ method.sweeps }} runs; requests per second also shows the range. "Slowest reply" is the worst single reply seen in any run.
- **Validity:** {{ method.validity_rule }}

